# pnpm + Prisma compatibility.
#
# pnpm's default content-addressable symlink layout (`isolated`) puts the
# generated Prisma client at a path the @prisma/client package's re-export
# shim can't always reach when the project is moved between Docker stages.
# The Prisma docs explicitly recommend `hoisted` for this combination:
#   https://pnpm.io/npmrc#node-linker
#   https://www.prisma.io/docs/orm/prisma-client/setup-and-configuration/generating-prisma-client#alternative-pnpm-with-node-linkerhoisted
#
# Hoisted means node_modules looks like an npm install — flat. Trade-off is
# slightly larger node_modules and looser dependency isolation; for a
# single-package backend that ships in a Docker image, neither matters.
node-linker=hoisted

# Build scripts are still gated by the `pnpm.onlyBuiltDependencies` allow-list
# in package.json, so postinstall hooks still only run for packages we trust.
